World Top Restaurants Data Analysis
Project Overview

This project performs Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on a dataset containing information about top restaurants around the world. The analysis focuses on restaurant ratings, Michelin stars, pricing, cuisine types, seating capacity, years of operation, and geographical distribution.

The goal is to uncover patterns and insights that help understand the characteristics of highly rated restaurants globally.

Dataset Features

The dataset includes the following attributes:

Restaurant Name
Country
Continent
Cuisine Type
Michelin Stars
Average Price (USD)
Rating
Seating Capacity
Years Operating
Established Year
Price Category

Technologies Used
Python
Pandas
Matplotlib
Seaborn

Analysis Performed
1. Data Loading & Exploration
Loaded dataset using Pandas.
Inspected dataset structure and columns.
Checked unique countries represented.
2. Country-wise Price Analysis
Visualized average restaurant prices across countries using bar charts.
3. Cuisine Type Analysis
Compared average prices among different cuisine types.
4. Michelin Star Distribution
Counted restaurants based on Michelin star ratings.
5. Restaurant Rating Distribution
Created histogram and KDE plots to understand rating distribution.
6. Price Category Analysis
Used boxplots to examine:
Average Price by Price Category
Rating by Price Category
7. Continental Distribution
Analyzed the number of restaurants across continents.
8. Average Price Distribution
Studied the spread of restaurant prices using histograms.
9. Correlation Analysis
Examined relationships among:
Rating
Average Price
Seating Capacity
Michelin Stars
Years Operating
Established Year
10. Correlation Heatmap
Visualized feature relationships using a heatmap.
